# Q2 Platform Review
{.lead} What shipped, what moved the numbers, and where we focus next.

---

## Summary
The platform had its strongest quarter yet. Adoption rose across every segment and the core workflow is measurably faster. Three numbers tell the story, and one decision follows from them.

- Onboarding completion climbed to 81 percent.
- Median time to first value fell by half.
- Support volume held flat despite more users.

---

## The numbers
```mdp:stats
Active teams: 1,240
Time to value: 3.5 days
Retention (90d): 88%
```

---

## What changed
We rebuilt the import pipeline, simplified the first run, and cut the setup checklist from nine steps to four. The result is a shorter path from sign-up to a working project.

---

## Recommendation
:::callout recommendation
Invest in the import pipeline next. It is the single biggest lever on time to value, and it unblocks the three largest deals in the pipeline.
:::

---

## Closing
The product is on a strong line. Holding this pace through Q3 puts the annual target within reach a quarter early.

> "This is the first quarter the product felt inevitable."
> {.cite} Internal review, Q2
